      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1912-07-13_WidnesExaminer_art0017" n="art0017">
        <head>BOWLING.</head>
        <p>BOWLING.</p>
        <p>BRITISH CROWN GREEN ASSOCIATION.</p>
        <p>THE COUNTY CHAMPIONSHIP. LANCASHIRE v. CHESHIRE.</p>
        <p>Pour of the counties affiliated to the British Crown Green Amateur Association turned out teams in the Crosfield Cup and County Championship on 'tSaturday, Lancashire •opposing Cheshire at Southport and Bowdon and Yorkshire meeting Derbyshire at New Mills and Halifax. The meetings were of a series to decide the fifth annual competition for the British ollampionship,in which Lancashire,Derbyshire,Cheshire, Staffordshire and Yorkshire meet each other in home- and-home matches, the aggregate to decide the winning county. The heaviest defeat was that inflicted upon W Flavell, of Winnington, who has previously won the gold medal for the best aggregate score by a Cheshire player in these competitions. Details : At Griffin Hotel Bowden HESHIRE. LANCASHIRE. O H Crosby, B'don V 2l A Gleave, Whitecross 15 J Dennison, Sale Q's 2l T Huraphries,RyPds... 11 S Holt, A-on-M l2 J Gleave, W'gton B H 21 A Hunt, Great Moor ll P Talbot, New-le-W... 21 L Mottershead, Sale 2O JW G Combes, R'2'k 21 A Prow, Linotype l7 J Grundy, Man &amp; S ... 21 M Harper, Congleton S Whitby, Win'ton P 17 C W Smith, Roebuck 21 T B Burgess, Win'ton 2l S Sladens, Within. ... 7 T Dale. A-on-M. N A Burke` A-on-M 2l F Whitehead, Ye OBG 13 Smith, Heatly GD l6 J Grundy, Lgh Rly 2l.</p>
        <p>219 202 Majority for Cheshire, 17 DERBYSHIRE V. YORKSHIRE.—At New Mills. Derbyshire At Halifax. Yorkshire</p>
      </div>
