        <p>With the holiday season at hand, our lady readers will be requiring something to protect their face and hands from the effects of exposure to the sun, sea. eater, &amp;c. One of the most famous emollients for this purpose, popular in all.parts of the civilised world, is Messrs. Beetham's La-rola, which not only prevents the injurious effects of the sum wind, hard water, &amp;c., but acts as a tonic and food to the delicate skin tissues. Unlike the majority of toilet preparations La-rola is sold at a price to suit all pockets and to enable our readers to test this, Messrs. Beetham and Son, the proprietors, are willing to send post free upon receipt of three penny stamps, a dainty box of samples containing a Bottle of " La-role," a Tube of Tooth Paste, Packet of Toilet Powder, also Rose Bloom, and a cake of deliciously scented toilet soap. Address to M. Beetham and Son, Cheltenham. '</p>
