        <p>HOWLEY B. V. ORFORD B. The Howleyites were on top form on Sian although they were up against Orford they en' third round with a 22 point victory to their Cr cwiet The Orford team had only four wins to tbe" ' on the individual games and they were lucky t° off with such a light defeat. .01 -- There were several sweeping victories for botilL'eflti and there were only two games worthy of c°';ocl These were the ones between J Wych (Orford) Mockon, M Llewellyn (Howley) and J re, In the game between Llewellyn and Bissell theit4iie were equal at 9 and 12 at the 17th end. The got his winning wood on the next eua thus wi. the odd point. 113 • ill d cIS o Mockon had the best of the first seven e° 6°,0 Wye] for he led by 9-2. Wych played a ce„r'ill game though from this point and eventually odd chalk, the game having extended over 17 0° 'Ote Sr. AUSTIN'S A V ST. AUSTIN'S B. pox' to The B team gained a brilliant victory by "4, Ito only two of their men having lost Itheir ger°:•als ' highest score of a defeated trundler on either ten. 13 0 tiled J Both captains won their contests J E Jeffere.,°s• se 13 Skipper beating W Brown 13-1 in nine erw,3 Wilkes B lost to the A captain, F Gray, by 104 ends. mole D 1' Percival (A) slackened off painfully' 0,00 t° with H Lindley for after having lead 10-3 at end he eventually lost by three chalks. t The B team are a strong force and will take shifting in this competition.</p>
