      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1912-07-13_WidnesExaminer_art0054" n="art0054">
        <head>FOR YOU</head>
        <p>FOR YOU</p>
        <p>there is such a handy remedy for digestive disorders as Beecham's Pills. No doubt there are other preparations that will afford some measure of relief, hut there are none more reliable and efficacious than the World's Household Medicine. Certain it is that no popu- lar remedy enioys such universal fame and, consequently, none is so easily obtainable. To have a box of Beecham's Pills in the house is to possess the means of obtaining immediate relief and to avoid the necessity of having to procure medicine at inopportune hours. So it is always wise to have Beecham's Pills handy. You are then prepared at any time to prevent, or cut' short, attacks of biliousness, indigestion, constipation, headache, and other ail- ments of the digestive system to which everyone is more or less liable. Look into your medicine supply to-day and make sure that</p>
