        <p>EDUCATION COMMITTEE.</p>
        <p>Business of the Next Meeting.</p>
        <p>The monthly meeting of the Warrington Edu Committee will be held at the Town Hall on :lb evening when the business to he considered will' the following :</p>
        <p>A PPOINTM ENT. Mr. John E. Morgan is r commended for appoint as headmaster of St. Barnabas' mixed school, at s mencing salary of £lBO. TEACHERS' PLACE OF RES I DENCE. It was noted that the Education Committee hsel approved and (adopted the resolution of the Sc Management Committed with regard to suggested ditions to be attached to the appointment of teachers in respect of place of residence and mina' period of service. Further consideration of the matter was adjourned the next meeting of the committee.</p>
        <p>THE RESULT OF DELAY. It was noted by the Sites and Buildings Cornini ttoeer that the Contractor for the extension ot the 13,91 Council school had withdrawn his tender of Noven3' last for the erection of the douche baths, owing to excessive advance in the prices of materials in meantime.</p>
        <p>It was decided to request the law Clerk to inform Local Government Board of this effect of their delay sanctioning the loan for this purpose, and to ask to furnish the committee with any explanation may be of such delay.</p>
