      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1912-07-13_WidnesExaminer_art0106" n="art0106">
        <head>Pure Indian Tea</head>
        <p>Pure Indian Tea</p>
        <p>A British Empire Product.</p>
        <p>Indian Tea is there- fore highly economical But moru. India pro- duces a large varety of teas. We can find deli- cate hill-grown Indian Ten for those of weak tiori, and full. led teas rinre</p>
        <p>and nfactures bh tea r seienti</p>
        <p>•alth. ,er t s tes- these .s and opinions summed up</p>
        <p>the Lanceg of the 7th Jinti'lry. 1911. and the Family DcMor of 24th December. 1911). The latter „paper emphasises the I'wonderful economy in u;e of Indian Tea.</p>
