        <p>WARRINGTON AND DISTRICT BOWLING ASSOCIATION. Individual Merit Championship. A Council meeting of the above Association was held at the Pelican Hotel, on Thursday evening, the chair- man being Mr George Ball, jun , the secretary, Mr J Wood, was also present and a fair number of members attended. After some discussion it was decided to leave the competition open far another week (nntil next Thursday). Only sullicieut games for next Saturday? July 13th, were drawn. The games are to be played on the Cemetery Hotel Green. Those who have entered for the " Harold Smith Cup Competition" are eligible to play in this r.ent, comretit iOll. OFFICIALS. It was decided to ask Mr It Trigger to act as gate- keeper. Mr George Ball. jun., was appointed the referee with Mr S Leigh as assistant. The draw resulted as follows :- 2.30 To 3.30 P.M. G Shaw, jun., Rylands v W Butterworth, Cemetery .1 Finch, Penketh v II ttothwell. Cemetery J Isherwood, Junior Conservatives v G Ball, sen , Cemetery A Siddall, Whitecross v J Roberts. Fearnbead H Mather, Cemetery v C Jordan, Cemetery J Baldwin, Cemetery v J Foster, Cemetery 3.30 To 430 P.M. R Knight, Cemetery v H Beunett, Junior Conservatives David Gleave, Fearnhead v A Scott, Cemetery R Sunderland, Junior Conservatives v H Ratclifie, Fearnhead H Rathbone, Cemetery v W Cottarn. Rylands W Rougbley, lta lands v W Barton, Cemetery 'l' Rigby, Bull's -Head v J Lodge, Cemetery 4.30 TO 530. Unsworth. Rylands v H Williams, Rylands T Ellison' junr., Whitecross v F Turner, Fen [ahead J Lister, RINI:Ids v E (Heave, Cemetery T Gregson' Penketh v J Langley, Rylands W T Woods, Cemetery v J Roberts, Cemetery A J Jones, Cemetery v J Appleton, Whitecross 5.30 TO 6.30. H Reunion, Whitcross 7 r Egerton, Whitecross G Ellison, Cemetery v John Bowyer, Pent, eth S Massey, Whitecross v E Povey, Rylands Joe Bowyer, Penketh v F Smith, Cemetery.</p>
