        <p>THURSDAY'S PROCEEDS. The gross proceeds on Thursday amounted to about £lOO more than for the corresponding day in 1910. The total was £339 15s. sd, wade up as follows : £ r. d Cockerels'... ... 19 15 1 Motor Cars 45 18 3 Joy Wheel 24 9 10 Jumping Horses... ... ... 29 14 3 Steam Yachts . 11 18 0- Hoop-la 11 5 4 Ring-la 5 9 5 Striker ... 116 3 Cocoanut Shy ... 918 3 Aunt Sully ... 618 10 Swings 1 18 0 *Alpine Railway ' ... 413 9 Shooting Jungle and flange ... 10 15 8 Juvenile Horses... 4 4 4 Dancing on the Green... 2 9 8 Pierrots 8 11 4 Doll Show ... 13 1 0 Flower Stall ... nl5 4 Children's Stall... ... •.. 6 19 10 Bar and Receipts at Knutsford-road and River Entrances ... 102 12 4 Camera Obs_cura.... 0 5 9 Cloak Room ... 019 7 Donkeys ... 2 7 1 Sundries ... 4 0 2 339 15 5 THE DOLL COMPETITION. The result of the doll competition was announced last night as follows Most suiiably dressed (over 18 years of age) 1, Mrs. Amos; 2, Miss Lediard; 3, Mrs. Daintith. Most suitably dressed (14 to 1(3 years of age), Miss J Solomon. Most suitably dressed (under 14 years of age), 1, Miss Dot is Ta3lor; 2, Miss Ida Pone; 3, Miss Veronica Malings. Most suitably dret:sed by persons employed in any of the drapery a, d other establishments in the town and district :—Mrs. The prize for the most original style of costume was awarded to Mrs. Powns with Miss Lakin second and a st.:ecial prize was awarded to Miss N. Atkinson. THE INSURANCE ACT. 'MEETING OF THE WARRINGTON COMMIITEE. The National Tnsuranre Act comes into (ores on Monday next. The first formal meeting of the Ptovi-ionsl Insurance Committee was held on Thurs- day evening, in the Council Chamber at the Town Dail, When there were 39 members present. His IV. rsh,p the Mayor was elected chairman for the life if the commi tee, which is until 13th July, 1913, or until the C,,mtnissiociers form a permanent committee. Sul,-cooduittees were appointed to deal with the administration of sanatoria benefits and other matt-re. Mr. A. T. Hallaway ;clef uty town clerk) and Mr. T. H. Spinks (assistant town, clerk) weie sppointed clerk and assistant clerk resrectively. The duties of the committee will be to administer , sanat •ria and medical benefits. In the case of all contributors, and in tie case of deposit contributors they will also administer maternity, disablement and sick benefit. Wthere c ntributors are members of an approved sccirty the last three named benefits will be administered by approved societies. • MR. JOHN BURNS AND ELECTORAL REFORM. Speaking on the second reading of the Franchis. and Regist rat i. it Bill in the Home of Commons on Thurs- day, Sir. John Burns said he did not believe there ass any danger to the cour ry in a further enfranchisement of the people. The trill was not a revolution ; it was a rrat;'-mAI sequence and complement of previous Reform 8,.15.</p>
